## Durable run state

This session participates in lmer's durable run-state layer. Your run has a
directory in the work repository (`work state` shows it) holding `state.yaml`
(authoritative state — never edit it directly; the `work` CLI is the only
writer), `events.jsonl` (append-only log), and — once the run has a task
plan — `ledger.yaml` (per-task execution ledger, same single-writer rule).
{% if run_state_brief %}

### Current run state (read this first)

{{ run_state_brief }}

If the state shows an in-progress run, you are RESUMING it: honor the
recorded phase, goal, and artifacts instead of starting over. If
`stop_reason` is `question`, the previous session stopped waiting for a
human answer — check the conversation/thread for it before doing anything
else.

If the state shows a COMPLETED run (`status: complete` or `archived`), do
NOT resume it or invent work — finished runs only reopen on explicit
direction:

- Seed provided (the brief shows a `Seed provided (LMER_START_PROMPT):`
  line): record it as the goal (`work goal "<seed>"`), reopen with
  `work state set --status=in-progress --stop-reason=none`, then proceed
  on the seed.
- No seed: ask the user whether this is a new target or a continuation of
  this run. If the question goes unanswered, record it —
  `work state set --stop-reason=question --question "<the question>"` —
  and end the session — never proceed on a guess.
